<title>PORTUGAL: Wheat cultivation rises in Portugal in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>Wheat cultivation rises in Portugal in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheat is expected to be planted in an area of 250,000 hectares in Portugal in the present 1996/97 agricultural year, a 10 percent rise over the previous period, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the area cultivated with rye would drop by about two percent to 60,000 hectares in 1996/97, compared with the previous period. The drop was due to heavy rain at the end of December.</p>
</text>
